    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1303">

                <pb facs="0886" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg770"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/48.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chargé O’Shaughnessy to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 22, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>735. Referring to Department’s 618, January 21. Many complaints are coming to
                    this Embassy regarding forced loans upon <pb facs="0887" n="771" xml:id="pg771"
                    /> American citizens. I have already advised Americans more or less in the sense
                    of Department’s 618, January 21, but I have the honor to respectfully suggest
                    that I be authorized to enter a formal protest with the Mexican de facto
                    government in the premises.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson O’Shaughnessy</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
